<title>USA: Midwest Cash Grain PM - Corn basis steady-weaker.</title>
<headline>Midwest Cash Grain PM - Corn basis steady-weaker.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Corn basis bids were weaker at several locations on Tuesday as sluggish export demand weighed on levels, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are hearing it (corn) is not moving in New Orleans,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>A sharp increase in the Chicago wheat elevator basis bid was noted. Dealers said the bid had been &quot;ridiculously low&quot; with elevators trying to avoid receiving disease-ridden old crop supplies.</p>
<p>Early signs that this year's crop may have relatively few disease problems prompted renewed buying interest, they said.  </p>
<p>Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures, cash $/bu.</p>
